00:50:52.880 --> 00:51:08.240
<v Ira Glass>Well, our program today about teenage girls comes to a close with this last story from radio producer Greg Whitehead, who lives in Massachusetts. This story is called "This Mindless Thing." Again, some content in this story may not be suitable for younger listeners.
<v Ira Glass>好的，我们今天关于少女的节目，就以广播制作人格雷格·怀特海德带来的最后一个故事结束，他住在马萨诸塞州。这个故事题为《这无心之物》。再次提醒，本节目的部分内容可能不适合年幼听众。

00:51:08.240 --> 00:51:41.660
<v Woman>I was 13, and he was 15. And we were going to go to the movies. We went to the Blue Star shopping center on Route 22 to see Live or Let Die. And I think his mother drove us. And we sat in the movie next to each other, and he didn't make a move. And nothing happened. And then his father came and picked us up and drove us back to his house.
<v Woman>当时我13岁，他15岁。我们打算去看电影。我们去了22号公路上的蓝星购物中心看《生死关头》。我想是他妈妈开车送我们去的。我们并排坐在电影院里，他什么举动也没有。什么都没发生。然后他爸爸来接我们，把我们送回了他家。

00:51:41.660 --> 00:52:09.340
<v Woman>So he said, "Do you want to come up to my room?" And as we went into his room, he closed the door and said, "We're not allowed to lock our doors in my house." So otherwise he would have locked the door.
<v Woman>于是他说：“你想上我房间坐坐吗？”当我们走进他房间时，他关上门说：“在我家，我们不准锁门。”否则他肯定会把门锁上的。

00:52:09.340 --> 00:52:15.340
<v Woman>This is really hard.
<v Woman>这真的很难说出口。

00:52:15.340 --> 00:52:45.670
<v Woman>So I don't know. He roamed around and was showing me stuff, and I was just being sort of polite. And showing me all his toys and junk and silly things that he had, and then proceeded to make the moves, make the big moves on me. And I was just very innocent. And he was very aggressive and just started kissing me and then just said, "Take off your shirt."
<v Woman>我不知道该怎么办。他在房间里晃来晃去，向我展示各种东西，我只是出于礼貌应付着。他给我看了他所有的玩具、杂物和那些傻玩意儿，接着就开始有所动作，对我动手动脚。我当时非常天真。他很有攻击性，开始吻我，然后直接说：“脱掉你的衬衫。”

00:52:45.670 --> 00:52:57.910
<v Woman>And so I'm sitting there thinking, well, the door is unlocked. And he said, "Well, you know--" And he had a little sister who was pestering us.
<v Woman>我坐在那儿心想，门没锁。他说，“嗯，你知道……”他有个小妹妹一直在打扰我们。

00:52:57.910 --> 00:53:24.870
<v Woman>So eventually I said, [UNINTELLIGIBLE PHRASE] And he's like, "Oh, no." And asks me do I want to see it. I did. And of course, I want to see it. I mean, I want to know what it looks like. But at the same time, I feel like I'm in this incredibly ominous-- this is a dangerous situation. It's pornographic. Now I know how much of a little girl I was. I was just 13. I mean, 13 is young.
<v Woman>所以最后我说，[无法理解的短语]。他就像是说，“哦，不。”并问我想不想看看那个东西。我想看。当然，我想看。我是说，我想知道它长什么样。但同时，我觉得自己置身于一种极其不详的氛围中——这是一种危险的情况。这是色情。现在我知道当时的我是多么像个小女孩。我才13岁。我是说，13岁还很小。

00:53:24.870 --> 00:53:35.530
<v Woman>But there it was, it was this mindless thing. And I thought, well [UNINTELLIGIBLE PHRASE] --I want to see it jump, this is what I have to do.
<v Woman>但它就在那儿，这件无心之物。我想，好吧[无法理解的短语]——我想看它跳动，这就是我必须做的。

00:53:35.530 --> 00:53:44.040
<v Woman>So yeah, so he whips it out. And we both sit and we look at it.
<v Woman>所以，是的，他把它掏了出来。我们两个就坐在那儿看着它。

00:53:44.040 --> 00:53:50.900
<v Woman>And he says, "Well, do you want to touch it?"
<v Woman>然后他说：“怎么样，你想摸摸看吗？”

00:53:50.900 --> 00:54:38.810
<v Woman>And I didn't want to, but I did to get to a safe place. It was just horrible and dirty. More dirty than anything I've ever done since, even trying to be dirty. It was clinical, and I felt like I was being experimented upon. And the worst thing was that I was so passive. And I did what I was told, because I was a good girl. It was like a game to him.
<v Woman>我其实不想，但我为了表现得“安全”一点还是摸了。那真是太恐怖、太肮脏了。比我之后做过的任何事都脏，即便是在试图做坏事的时候。那过程像是一场实验，我感觉自己像个实验品。最糟糕的是，我当时太被动了。我照他说的做了，因为我是个乖女孩。对他来说，那就像一场游戏。

00:54:38.810 --> 00:55:11.010
<v Woman>Now that I'm older, now that I think about it, it was a game. It wasn't playful. It was a very sophisticated game. It was a game. And it wasn't loving to coerce someone or to seduce someone-- or to seduce a little girl. It was as if he were 40.
<v Woman>现在我长大了，回头想想，那确实是一场游戏。那并不单纯。那是一场非常老练的游戏。那是个游戏。诱惑某人，诱惑一个小女孩，这并非出于爱。他表现得就像个40岁的成年人。

00:55:11.010 --> 00:55:27.130
<v Woman>So here was this mindless thing. And he would look at me and think that I had been curious. "Want to see it jump?" So he could make it move. And flop around all by itself.
<v Woman>所以这就是那个无心之物。他会看着我，以为我很好奇。“想看它跳吗？”所以他能让它动起来。让它自己在那儿晃荡。

00:55:27.130 --> 00:55:29.950
<v Woman>[INTERPOSING VOICES]
<v Woman>[嘈杂声]

00:55:29.950 --> 00:55:54.440
<v Ira Glass>--mindless thing, but it has a mind of its own and a body of its own. It sort of moved around. And I was just appalled. I had no idea that this was what happened, that you could make it move all by itself, without touching it. And that it just stood up, stood straight up. It was like his little ventriloquist dummy that he could make talk to me.
<v Ira Glass>——无心之物，但它却有自己的思想，有自己的身体。它自己在那里动来动去。我简直震惊了。我根本不知道会发生这种事，不知道你竟然可以让它在不接触的情况下自己动起来。它竟然直接站了起来，笔直地竖着。就像是他腹语表演的木偶，他可以让它跟我对话。

00:55:54.440 --> 00:56:04.030
<v Ira Glass>It wasn't playful. It wasn't erotic. It wasn't loving. We put our clothes back on.
<v Ira Glass>那不调皮。那不色情。那不充满爱。我们重新穿上了衣服。

00:56:04.030 --> 00:56:16.260
<v Ira Glass>My mother came and picked us up. And I walked outside on his nice suburban lawn. I just wanted to get out of there. And his mother was there, and my mother was talking to his mother. And I stared at our mothers.
<v Ira Glass>我妈妈来接我们了。我走在他家漂亮的郊区草坪上。我只想离开那儿。他妈妈在那里，我妈妈正和他妈妈说话。我盯着我们的母亲们看。

00:56:16.260 --> 00:56:18.900
<v Ira Glass>[INTERPOSING VOICES]
<v Ira Glass>[嘈杂声]

00:56:18.900 --> 00:56:37.710
<v Ira Glass>If they knew what had been going on. I just wanted to get out of there, to get to a safe place. But then I knew I could never tell anyone what had happened. So I could never be in a safe place.
<v Ira Glass>如果她们知道发生了什么。我只想离开那儿，去一个安全的地方。但我知道我永远不能告诉任何人发生了什么。所以我永远无法身处安全之地。

